     "id": "requirements-analyst.quality-standards.independent-benefit-anchored-every",
     "verdict": "contradicted",
     "evidence": "**US-004 (P2)** Employee: a single list and total of everything I claimed over a date range. *Both employee tickets.* / **US-005 (P2, blocked on Phase 4)** Manager: my team's spend for the current period. / **US-007 (P3)** Anyone with report access: the same totals shown as by-category and by-month charts on a dashboard page. \u2014 These stories shown in Phase 5's planned set lack explicit value statements (the \"so that\"). US-003 does include \"so it can be chased,\" but US-004, US-005, US-006, and US-007 do not name the benefit."
    },
    {
     "id": "requirements-analyst.what-reject.assumptions-hidden-requirements",
     "verdict": "reflected",
     "evidence": "Each gets an explicit assumption or an open question \u2014 never a silent guess. / I record as an assumption the consequence nobody has stated \u2014 that rate is fixed at *filing* day, so a total will not match an accountant re-converting at month-end rate. The \"to the penny\" promise is therefore *penny-match against the Tally run*, not against an external re-conversion. I would state that explicitly so it is not discovered in QA. / Functional requirements will carry the Phase 3 rulings \u2014 period keyed on date incurred, approved-and-paid only, company currency via stored converted amount, no re-rounding, archived categories included, zero-months render as zero"
    },
    {
     "id": "requirements-analyst.what-reject.requirements-can-t-be",
     "verdict": "reflected",
     "evidence": "I would not accept \"like the big expense tools\" as a requirement \u2014 it is unbuildable and untestable. / confirm every story has a pass/fail independent test / Success criteria will be measurable and tied to the evidence: finance month-end totalling time drops from the reported two-to-three hours to under fifteen minutes; report totals equal run totals in 100% of comparisons; the reporting-tagged ticket rate falls."
    }
   ]
